## Running the Project

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/techie-code/Changing-Health-Age-Relationships-Across-the-Pandemic-Insights-from-Explainable-Neural-Networks.git
```

Move into the project directory:

```bash
cd Changing-Health-Age-Relationships-Across-the-Pandemic-Insights-from-Explainable-Neural-Networks
```

Launch Jupyter Notebook or JupyterLab:

```bash
jupyter notebook
```

The main analysis is contained in:

```text
Dissertation_Pre_Post_Comparison.ipynb
```

---

## Main Python Libraries

The notebooks use standard Python statistical and machine-learning libraries, including tools for:

* Data manipulation and numerical computation
* Statistical modelling
* Machine learning
* Neural networks
* Explainable AI
* Data visualization

The exact environment may depend on the notebook version and installed package versions.

---

## Interpretation and Limitations

Several limitations should be considered when interpreting the analysis.

NHANES is observational and cross-sectional, so the results identify statistical and predictive associations rather than causal relationships.

Differences between pre-pandemic and post-pandemic models may reflect several factors, including:

* Changes in the sampled population
* Measurement differences
* Sampling variability
* Changes in health patterns
* Model uncertainty
* Broader temporal changes unrelated to the pandemic itself

Consequently, changes between periods should not automatically be attributed directly to COVID-19 or pandemic-related effects.

